\ The word-body counterpart of metadata_only_nonprelude_reach: the hash-buried
\ quotation lives inside a word definition instead of the entry instructions.
\ `floor` is a module word reachable only through that quotation, so the
\ freezer never compiles it, and the interpreted call would run its empty
\ metadata-image body silently. The build must reject this shape and direct
\ the user to --emit-runtime-image.
use { floor: } "math" ;
runner: ( x -- y ) [ H{ go: [ floor ] } go: @get call ] ;
3.7 runner
.
